WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:02.968
-You were telling me backstage,
and I don't know if you wanted

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:04.567
to talk about this,
but I wanted to bring it up

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:06.968
that you were thinking about
getting into something new.

00:00:06.968 --> 00:00:09.968
And it just intrigued me because
it didn't seem like something

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:12.601
that Kiefer Sutherland
would get into.

00:00:12.601 --> 00:00:13.968
-I wanted to --

00:00:13.968 --> 00:00:17.434
Well, I want
to get into farming.

00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:21.767
I started -- There we go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:23.167
There's three farmers
out there.

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:24.968
-Three farmers out there,
but, you --

00:00:24.968 --> 00:00:26.734
-And I'm not a farmer.
I'm learning.

00:00:26.734 --> 00:00:29.267
I'm reading books about it.

00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:30.834
I started cooking.

00:00:30.834 --> 00:00:32.834
Well, I have children
and I have grandchildren,

00:00:32.834 --> 00:00:33.968
so I took cooking lessons,

00:00:33.968 --> 00:00:35.234
because I didn't want
to kill them

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:37.367
accidentally with an undercooked
turkey or something.

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:38.567
-Yeah. Yeah, of course.
Yeah, of course.

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:39.634
-And I fell in love with it.

00:00:39.634 --> 00:00:43.133
And during the pandemic,
I cooked a lot.

00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:46.234
And I got into the produce
that that I was using for food.

00:00:46.234 --> 00:00:50.033
And I thought, "Well, I've seen
a couple of documentaries,

00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:52.501
and maybe I'd like
to actually try growing

00:00:52.501 --> 00:00:54.067
some of this food," and --

00:00:54.067 --> 00:00:55.634
-I can't see you in, like,
overalls

00:00:55.634 --> 00:00:58.501
and really going for it
and, like, getting a tractor.

00:00:58.501 --> 00:01:01.200
I mean --
-Very, very few people can.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.601
-Yeah. Do you have
a green thumb?

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:04.434
-Mainly my family. No.

00:01:04.434 --> 00:01:07.067
And that's the hard part,
that's why I have all the books.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:10.534
No. Whatever the opposite color
of green is the thumb

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:11.868
that I have.
-Yeah.

00:01:11.868 --> 00:01:16.334
-When my daughter was about
4 years old,

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:19.367
we went to the hardware store
and got a bunch

00:01:19.367 --> 00:01:23.734
of different seeds and looking
for the easiest thing to grow.

00:01:23.734 --> 00:01:25.801
And those are daisies,
because they're weeds.

00:01:25.801 --> 00:01:27.801
And we planted them
all over the house,

00:01:27.801 --> 00:01:29.167
and I thought,
"How nice this is gonna be

00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:30.801
when she goes to school
next year,

00:01:30.801 --> 00:01:32.601
we'll be picking
these fresh daisies."

00:01:32.601 --> 00:01:33.901
Seven years later, nothing.

00:01:33.901 --> 00:01:35.601
Nothing grew.

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:37.033
-You really have no experience

00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:39.100
and no green thumb at all?
-No, the worst,

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.701
the worst.
-But I think that you

00:01:40.701 --> 00:01:43.033
like a challenge, so I think --
-I do.

00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:44.601
And I also want to --

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:47.534
I want livestock, which is even
more challenging --

00:01:47.534 --> 00:01:48.701
-This is where you get
out of control.

00:01:48.701 --> 00:01:50.267
What do you mean, now?

00:01:50.267 --> 00:01:51.868
Like, what kind of livestock
are you talking here?

00:01:51.868 --> 00:01:54.534
-Well, I want I want
two donkeys.

00:01:54.534 --> 00:01:58.334
I want some chickens.
I want a couple of goats.

00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:00.434
I'm going the whole 100 yards.

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:01.567
-I love that you're doing that.

00:02:01.567 --> 00:02:03.033
What are you gonna do
with the donkey?

00:02:03.033 --> 00:02:06.267
-I'm gonna walk him.

00:02:06.267 --> 00:02:07.501
-Walk a donkey?

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:11.901
-Well, anybody can walk a dog,
right?

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:14.701
I mean, if you could walk
a donkey, would that not be fun?

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.501
-No -- Well, if I could walk
a donkey?

00:02:16.501 --> 00:02:18.267
-Yeah.
-Yeah. I mean, yeah,

00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:19.801
I can't wait to ask you.

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:21.300
I can't wait to see
what happens in six months.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.033
-Donkeys are
incredibly kind animals.

00:02:23.033 --> 00:02:25.868
They're a lot nicer than horses.

00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:29.701
And they're just --
they're really loving.

00:02:29.701 --> 00:02:31.701
-So this is this is --
I think this is gonna --

00:02:31.701 --> 00:02:33.067
I think you're really gonna
do this.

00:02:33.067 --> 00:02:34.367
-Well, I am definitely
gonna do it.

00:02:34.367 --> 00:02:35.434
I don't know if I'm gonna
be successful,

00:02:35.434 --> 00:02:36.901
but I'm definitely
gonna do it.

00:02:36.901 --> 00:02:38.367
-What inspired you besides --

00:02:38.367 --> 00:02:41.167
I mean, do you have your land
or your neighbors, or?

00:02:41.167 --> 00:02:44.167
-Well, I've raised cattle
over the course of my life.

00:02:44.167 --> 00:02:48.100
I had a few different ranches,
and I did that very seriously

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.934
with a great friend of mine
named John English.

00:02:49.934 --> 00:02:53.501
And I just --
I really missed the country.

00:02:53.501 --> 00:02:55.767
I spent a lot of time,
certainly through "24."

00:02:55.767 --> 00:02:58.567
I spent all of that time
in Los Angeles

00:02:58.567 --> 00:02:59.968
and through
"Designated Survivor"

00:02:59.968 --> 00:03:01.467
and now "Rabbit Hole."

00:03:01.467 --> 00:03:04.834
That was all in the city
of Toronto and I missed nature.

00:03:04.834 --> 00:03:07.501
-You just mentioned "24",
and I know the fans --

00:03:07.501 --> 00:03:09.033
you were nice --

00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:10.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.167
-Thank you, thank you.

00:03:12.167 --> 00:03:13.934
-We don't have time
for this, Chloe.

00:03:13.934 --> 00:03:15.801
I love it.

00:03:15.801 --> 00:03:17.701
You've been on the show
so many times for that,

00:03:17.701 --> 00:03:19.300
and thank you for coming on,
being a guest.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:23.834
Fans of "24" are always
wondering on the Internet,

00:03:23.834 --> 00:03:25.234
like, "Will you bring it back?

00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:28.234
Will there be some type
of '24' spinoff?"

00:03:28.234 --> 00:03:29.734
I mean, it's such
a great premise.

00:03:29.734 --> 00:03:32.133
-Well, the thing that --
I mean, I've always felt

00:03:32.133 --> 00:03:34.667
that the show was
the great star, right?

00:03:34.667 --> 00:03:37.467
The idea of a thriller
in real time,

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:39.601
that's just special.

00:03:39.601 --> 00:03:43.133
And it should go on forever
with me or without me.

00:03:43.133 --> 00:03:44.734
-Well, let me just say
something.

00:03:44.734 --> 00:03:46.667
You, my friend,
were the star of that, I mean.

00:03:46.667 --> 00:03:48.968
-That's very --
That's very nice.

00:03:48.968 --> 00:03:51.133
-There's no one
that could do it like you.

00:03:51.133 --> 00:03:52.934
You were unbelievable.
-Thank you.

00:03:52.934 --> 00:03:54.968
-But I agree that --
-But if they wrote it,

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:58.934
if -- this is so unfair
to -- Howard Gordon's

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:00.200
gonna kill me for this,

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.968
and he was the lead writer
of the last, well,

00:04:02.968 --> 00:04:05.400
the last seven seasons of "24."

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:08.934
And but if everybody came up
with a great idea,

00:04:08.934 --> 00:04:10.400
I would not be
the person to say,

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.934
"no, I would not be the reason
that it didn't come back."

00:04:12.934 --> 00:04:14.767
-That's what all I wanted
to hear.

00:04:14.767 --> 00:04:16.767
That's all I want to hear.

00:04:16.767 --> 00:04:18.100
I loved it.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:19.968
I used to tune in every week
and I go, "Oh my gosh,"

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:21.300
because you're living --

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:23.734
I'm living your hour with you
until we get to "24."

00:04:23.734 --> 00:04:25.634
It was so well done and great.
-Thank you.

00:04:25.634 --> 00:04:26.801
-I think I told you last time,

00:04:26.801 --> 00:04:28.467
because I ended up
buying the DVD box set,

00:04:28.467 --> 00:04:30.567
and I lent it to my friend
at the same time

00:04:30.567 --> 00:04:34.267
to watch it, as well.
And he lost one of the DVDs.

00:04:34.267 --> 00:04:36.133
So I missed like
three hours of "24."

00:04:36.133 --> 00:04:37.300
That's -- You can't do that.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:38.601
-I'll send them to you.
-You will?

00:04:38.601 --> 00:04:40.000
-Yes.
-That's a friend right there.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.968
Thank you, buddy.
I appreciate that.

00:04:41.968 --> 00:04:45.601
All right. Put a little pressure
out there just for that "24."

00:04:45.601 --> 00:04:47.834
But let's talk about
"Rabbit Hole" here.

00:04:47.834 --> 00:04:49.734
I only saw the first episode,
and I'm hooked.

00:04:49.734 --> 00:04:51.501
It's fantastic.

00:04:51.501 --> 00:04:52.801
It's a thriller.

00:04:52.801 --> 00:04:55.033
It's what you want to see
Kiefer Sutherland come in and do

00:04:55.033 --> 00:04:56.601
and kick butt and figure out.

00:04:56.601 --> 00:04:58.067
There's explosions,
there's action.

00:04:58.067 --> 00:05:01.501
I liked -- There's one scene
where you're delivering a box,

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:03.133
you're dressed as the delivery
guy, and you're like,

00:05:03.133 --> 00:05:04.334
"I'm delivering this box here."

00:05:04.334 --> 00:05:05.968
And the guy's like,
"You got to sign."

00:05:05.968 --> 00:05:07.234
You go, "Oh, okay.

00:05:07.234 --> 00:05:09.267
I'll just -- can you
hold this box for a second?"

00:05:09.267 --> 00:05:10.300
And he goes, "Yeah."

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:11.434
And then you pull
some switch and go,

00:05:11.434 --> 00:05:13.300
"You're holding a bomb."
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:14.367
-It was so good.

00:05:14.367 --> 00:05:16.300
-It felt really
familiar, that line.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:17.400
-It was so good.

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:18.868
-I go, "Oh, I'm hooked, man."

00:05:18.868 --> 00:05:20.467
I loved it.

00:05:20.467 --> 00:05:22.234
How do we talk about,
how do we describe

00:05:22.234 --> 00:05:23.467
what "Rabbit Hole" is about?

00:05:23.467 --> 00:05:26.200
-I play a character
named John Weir,

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.234
who is involved
in corporate espionage,

00:05:28.234 --> 00:05:30.267
which is actually a real thing.

00:05:30.267 --> 00:05:32.200
And he's in the middle
of an operation

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:34.234
that goes terribly,
terribly wrong.

00:05:34.234 --> 00:05:35.968
And he literally goes
from the hunter

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:38.234
to the hunted
in a matter of moments.

00:05:38.234 --> 00:05:40.267
And the rest of the season
is him trying to figure out

00:05:40.267 --> 00:05:41.501
who's doing it to him,

00:05:41.501 --> 00:05:43.033
why are they doing it to him,

00:05:43.033 --> 00:05:45.400
and how does he clear his name
and save his life?

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:47.400
-Yeah, it's fantastic.
You're great in it

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:48.501
as you are.
-Thank you.

00:05:48.501 --> 00:05:49.701
-Please come back,
I want to know more

00:05:49.701 --> 00:05:50.734
about the farm, too,
when you come back.

00:05:50.734 --> 00:05:52.300
-I'll have pictures.

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:53.567
-I want to show a clip.

00:05:53.567 --> 00:05:55.133
Here's Kiefer Sutherland
in "Rabbit Hole."

00:05:55.133 --> 00:05:56.667
Take a look at this.

00:05:56.667 --> 00:05:58.968
-Where are you taking her?

00:05:58.968 --> 00:06:00.634
What's your precinct?

00:06:00.634 --> 00:06:02.734
What are the charges?

00:06:02.734 --> 00:06:03.934
This woman has done nothing,

00:06:03.934 --> 00:06:04.968
and they're arresting her.
[ Car horn honks ]

00:06:04.968 --> 00:06:06.033
-What are you doing?

00:06:06.033 --> 00:06:07.667
-[Bleep] I have it all
on camera.

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:09.868
-Answer him.
-I see you.

00:06:09.868 --> 00:06:13.667
We see you, we see you.
-Back off!

00:06:13.667 --> 00:06:15.501
-We see you, we see you.

00:06:15.501 --> 00:06:17.501
-We see you.
-Hey, we see you.

00:06:17.501 --> 00:06:18.801
-We see you, you son of a --

00:06:18.801 --> 00:06:21.767
-We can see you.

00:06:21.767 --> 00:06:22.767
-We see you!

00:06:22.767 --> 00:06:23.767
-Are you ready?
-For what?

00:06:23.767 --> 00:06:25.033
-We see you!
-Ready or not.

00:06:25.033 --> 00:06:27.100
Gun, gun, gun!
[ People screaming ]

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:28.267
-We see you!

00:06:28.267 --> 00:06:32.133
[ Screaming continues ]

00:06:32.701 --> 00:06:35.567
[ Indistinct shouting ]

00:06:35.567 --> 00:06:37.501
[ Screaming continues ]
-Yeah, that's what

00:06:37.501 --> 00:06:39.100
I'm talking about.

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:41.000
Kiefer Sutherland, everybody.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:44.901
"Rabbit Hole" premieres
this Sunday on Paramount+.

00:06:44.901 --> 00:06:46.267
-Jimin joins us after the break.

00:06:46.267 --> 00:06:47.300
Stick around.

